\section{CFG Construction from AST/IR}\label{sec:cfg-construction}

Constructing a CFG from an AST or high-level IR involves identifying basic blocks and connecting them with edges.

\subsection{Algorithm}\label{sec:cfg-algorithm}

\begin{algorithm}[H]
\caption{CFG Construction}\label{alg:cfg-construction}
\begin{algorithmic}[1]
\Function{BuildCFG}{$\mathrm{stmts}$}
  \State $\mathrm{leaders} \gets \{\mathrm{stmts}[0]\}$
  \For{each statement $s$ in $\mathrm{stmts}$}
    \If{$s$ is a branch target}
      \State $\mathrm{leaders} \gets \mathrm{leaders} \cup \{s\}$
    \EndIf
    \If{$s$ is a branch or jump}
      \State $\mathrm{leaders} \gets \mathrm{leaders} \cup \{\mathrm{next}(s)\}$
    \EndIf
  \EndFor
  \State $\mathrm{blocks} \gets \{\}$
  \For{each leader $l$ in $\mathrm{leaders}$}
    \State $\mathrm{block} \gets \{l\}$
    \State $s \gets \mathrm{next}(l)$
    \While{$s \notin \mathrm{leaders}$}
      \State $\mathrm{block} \gets \mathrm{block} \cup \{s\}$
      \State $s \gets \mathrm{next}(s)$
    \EndWhile
    \State $\mathrm{blocks} \gets \mathrm{blocks} \cup \{\mathrm{block}\}$
  \EndFor
  \State \Comment{Add edges based on branches and fall-through}
  \State \Return $\mathrm{blocks}$
\EndFunction
\end{algorithmic}
\end{algorithm}

\subsection{Structured Control Flow}\label{sec:structured-cfg}

For structured programs (if/else, while, for), the CFG has a regular structure:

\begin{verbatim}
  // Source:
  if (cond) {
    x = 1;
  } else {
    x = 2;
  }
  y = x + 1;

  // CFG:
  // B1: if (cond) -> B2 (true), B3 (false)
  // B2: x = 1 -> B4
  // B3: x = 2 -> B4
  // B4: y = x + 1
\end{verbatim}

\subsection{Unstructured Control Flow}\label{sec:unstructured-cfg}

For unstructured programs (goto, break, continue), the CFG may have arbitrary edges:

\begin{verbatim}
  // Source:
  loop:
    x = x + 1;
    if (x > 10) goto done;
    goto loop;
  done:
    return x;

  // CFG:
  // B1: x = x + 1; if (x > 10) -> B2 (true), B3 (false)
  // B2: return x
  // B3: goto B1
\end{verbatim}

