\section{Entry and Exit Nodes}\label{sec:entry-exit}

A CFG has a distinguished \emph{entry node} (the first block executed) and one or more \emph{exit nodes} (blocks that return or halt).

\subsection{Single Entry, Single Exit}\label{sec:seSE}

For analysis purposes, it is convenient to have a single entry and a single exit:
\begin{itemize}
  \item Add an \emph{entry block} with an unconditional edge to the original entry.
  \item Add an \emph{exit block} with edges from all return/halt blocks.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Multiple Exits}\label{sec:multiple-exits}

Functions with multiple return statements have multiple exit blocks. For analysis, these are typically merged into a single virtual exit.

