\subsection{Post-Dominance}\label{sec:post-dominance}

\begin{definition}[Post-Dominance]\label{def:post-dominance}
Block $D$ \emph{post-dominates} block $N$ if every path from $N$ to the exit must pass through $D$.
\end{definition}

Post-dominance is used for:
\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Control dependence.} Block $B$ is control-dependent on block $A$ if $A$ post-dominates the successor of $B$ but not $B$ itself.
  \item \textbf{Speculation safety.} An instruction can be speculatively executed if it is post-dominated by its original position.
  \item \textbf{Predication.} Instructions in post-dominated blocks can be converted to predicated instructions.
\end{itemize}

