Before inserting the increment, contracting the fresh block
recovers precisely the old paths and incoming value choices.
Preserving the terminator slot matters when two switch cases
originally share a destination. With adjacency handles, the
graph edit is constant time apart from visiting the destination's
phis and updating or recomputing analyses. A pass that rewrites
several edges should collect their original identities first,
rather than treating newly created edges as independent requests.

\section{Summary and Further Reading}\label{sec:summary-55}

The control-flow graph is the foundational data structure for program analysis and optimization. Basic blocks partition the program into linear sequences; edges represent control flow. Dominance, reachability, and dominance frontiers are structural properties that enable efficient analysis and transformation.

For further reading, we recommend Muchnick's comprehensive treatment~\cite{muchnick1997}, the classic paper by Allen~\cite{allen1970}, and the Lengauer--Tarjan algorithm~\cite{lengauer1979}.
